	abstract = {The research framework focuses on embedding technology in multi-tenant SaaS operations to automate administrative workflows with high variance. The combined use of intelligent process automation (IPA) and robotic process automation (RPA) and machine learning (ML) in hybrid rule-learning pipelines. We describe cloud-native architectural patterns microservices, containers/Kubernetes, event streaming, and service meshes that can isolate tenant data, and enable elastic scaling of model services and workflow engines. In terms of methodology, we use NLP to manage document and ticket flows, process mining to discover and optimize execution paths, reinforcement learning for tuning execution policies, and computer vision to automatically intake documents. These elements are assembled utilizing domain-based design and API gateway orchestration. Zero-trust access fetters, privacy-preserving computation patterns, data lineage and explanation techniques like LIME and SHAP permit auditable decisions are first-class governance and safety concerns. The systems run in a cloud-native architecture where adapters on the fabric interface with legacy systems to achieve integration across ERPs, CRMs, and other such systems using event sourcing, CDC, etc. It supports ensuring consistency and observability while retaining human-in-the-loop capabilities. Helpful metrics to measure impact include cycle time reduction, cost per ticket, and tenant-level scalability. The main contribution is an engineeringfocused synthesis emphasizing deployable patterns, performance tuning and operational resilience at the expense of novel algorithms to make AI a safe, interoperable and scalable orchestrator of B2B SaaS admin automation. © 2026 IEEE.},
