	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105026246644?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {As the real estate market grows increasingly complex and fintech advances rapidly, traditional real estate investment risk assessment methods no longer meet modern investment decision-making requirements in terms of data processing capabilities, analytical precision, and decision support. This study aims to construct a fintech-based intelligent real estate investment risk assessment and decision support system to achieve intelligent risk evaluation and optimized decision-making.At the hardware architecture level, the system employs a high-performance server cluster configuration. This includes dual-socket Intel Xeon processors for high-speed computation, NVIDIA A100 GPUs to accelerate deep learning operations, 384GB of high-capacity memory to support real-time data processing, NVMe solid-state drive arrays to ensure high-speed I/O performance, and 10Gbps network interconnects to enable high-speed communication between clusters. At the software architecture level, the system is built on a distributed microservices architecture. It utilizes the SpringCloud framework for service decoupling and load balancing, employs a three-tier design comprising presentation, business, and data layers, stores massive unstructured data via a MongoDB cluster, leverages a Redis cluster for high-speed caching services, and ensures environment consistency through Docker containerization. Kubernetes is deployed for container orchestration and service governance.At the algorithmic level, the system innovatively applies LSTM-Attention networks for risk feature modeling and employs deep reinforcement learning algorithms to optimize investment decision strategies, enabling deep mining and feature extraction from multidimensional real estate market data. Research findings demonstrate that through coordinated hardware-software optimization, the system achieves a 92.3% risk assessment accuracy rate in practical applications (a 15.6% improvement over traditional methods), reduces assessment response time to 15 milliseconds (a 98.75% improvement), and attains a concurrent processing capacity of 8,000 QPS (a 900% improvement).The system further offers risk alerts, portfolio optimization, and market trend analysis, providing comprehensive support for investment decisions. This research establishes a new technical paradigm for real estate investment risk management, holding significant implications for advancing digital transformation in the sector. This deeply integrated hardware-software system design not only ensures high performance and reliability but also provides valuable reference for developing similar fintech systems. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).},
