	abstract = {In response to the industry pain points existing in the current digital transformation of university education, such as the prominent existence of multi-source heterogeneous data islands, fragmented data governance system, insufficient scalability of the traditional monolithic architecture, and weak ability to mine the value of educational data, this paper designs and implements a university data governance and intelligent analysis system based on microservice architecture. The system adopts domain-driven design to complete the microservice domain division and the construction of cloud-native architecture, and builds a full-chain university data governance system covering data integration, standard control, quality governance, and security compliance. At the same time, it integrates and improves machine learning models such as XGBoost, optimized LSTM, and lightweight BERT, and realizes core intelligent analysis functions such as academic risk warning, student growth profile, enrollment and employment trend prediction, and campus public opinion risk identification. The experimental and pilot application results based on the 3-year full-scale real business data set of a provincial university show that this system can achieve a 62% improvement in the efficiency of batch synchronization of multi-source heterogeneous data, stable real-time data synchronization delay within 200ms, and an accuracy rate of data quality rule identification of 98.3%; in the core intelligent analysis models, the AUC value of the academic risk warning model reaches 0.957, an increase of 4.2 percentage points compared to the traditional XGBoost model, the average relative error of enrollment and employment trend prediction is reduced to 3.12%, and the accuracy rate of campus public opinion sentiment classification reaches 96.8%; in the 1000 concurrent scenario, the average response time of the system interface is less than 180ms, and the service availability reaches 99.95%. This sys