	abstract = {With the rapid pace of digital transformation, enterprises are facing significant challenges in integrating modern cloud-based platforms with legacy enterprise systems. Workday, as a leading cloud-based ERP platform, offers powerful capabilities for human capital and financial management, yet its integration with legacy on-premise applications and heterogeneous cloud platforms often results in data silos, inconsistent workflows, and high operational complexity. To achieve this, a hybrid methodology is proposed, combining the evolutionary mating optimization (EMO) algorithm for optimal data mapping and workflow orchestration with quantum deep neural network (QDNN) for intelligent data fusion and predictive analytics across Workday, legacy, and cloud platforms. The EMO algorithm ensures efficient alignment of heterogeneous system schemas and reduces integration overhead, while the QDNN learns complex patterns in multi-source enterprise data to enable accurate forecasting and anomaly detection. The proposed model adopts a microservices-based design, supporting modular expansion, real-time processing, and multi-terminal access. Experimental validation was carried out in a simulated enterprise environment where the optimized framework demonstrated a 32 % improvement in data synchronization speed, 27 % reduction in integration latency, and 21 % improvement in predictive accuracy compared to conventional middleware-based solutions. © 2025 IEEE.},
